  "worked_solution": "The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3+(3)(-1) & -1+(3)(2) & 9+(3)(4)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
